Krita Nova 85 - Composer: pie menus, cursor trackers, temporary switches, rotation selector

Native versions of Shortcut Composer's features (patch 84 bundles the Python
plugin, which cannot run on Android), in libs/ui/nova/KisNovaComposer:

- pie menus: Tools, Blending Modes, Brush Presets of a tag (with a "Tag..."
  slice and a Brush Preset Tag pie), Opacity, and the Composer menu that
  opens all of them plus the rotation selector, eraser and alpha lock;
  hold, point at a slice, release; or tap, then tap a slice (Esc, the
  middle or outside closes it). The current choice is tinted.
- cursor trackers: hold and drag - brush size (log scale, 150 px doubles
  it), opacity and flow (400 px for 0-100 %), active layer (every 40 px up
  / down), undo history (every 30 px left undoes, right redoes); the value
  shows in a floating message; applied at most every 30 ms.
- temporary switches: eraser, alpha lock, Move, Transform and Color Sampler
  tools - on while held, back on release; a tap toggles instead.
- rotation selector: a dial; the pointer's angle around it is the canvas
  rotation, snapping to every 15 degrees within 4; tapped, it stays open:
  drag on it, tap its middle to reset the rotation.

Triggers:
- keyboard: Configure Krita > Keyboard Shortcuts > "Krita Nova Composer"
  (krita/novacomposer.action, no defaults): hold the key and move, release;
- canvas input: Configure Krita > Canvas Input Settings > "Krita Nova
  Composer" (KisNovaComposerAction): any mouse / pen button (the pen's side
  button), key, or touch gesture; the bundled profiles open the Composer
  menu with a five-finger tap (custom profiles need it added);
- the Brush Panel: a Composer button under the pop-up palette button.

The pies and the dial are child widgets drawn over the main window.

